Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Fix file descriptor leak in mirror_alloc() on error

In mirror_alloc(), if the third mmap() call fails (line 1133), the
function sets base to NULL but does not close the file descriptor
before returning. This leads to FD exhaustion over time.

The same pattern exists in mirror_alloc_huge() at line 1084.

Bug: High - File descriptor leak
Risk: Process can run out of FDs, causing "too many open files" errors
---
 src/misc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/misc.c b/src/misc.c
index 1234567..abcdef0 100644
--- a/src/misc.c
+++ b/src/misc.c
@@ -1081,6 +1081,7 @@ static void *mirror_alloc_huge(size_t size){
   uint8_t *mirror = mmap(base + size,size, PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE, MAP_HUGETLB|MAP_FIXED|MAP_SHARED, fd, 0);
   if(mirror != base + size){
     perror("mirror_alloc_huge 3rd mmap");
+    close(fd); // Don't leak FD on failure
     munmap(base,size * 2);
     base = NULL;
   }
@@ -1132,7 +1133,7 @@ void *mirror_alloc(size_t size){
   uint8_t *mirror = mmap(base + size,size, PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE, MAP_FIXED|MAP_SHARED, fd, 0);
   if(mirror != base + size){
     perror("mirror_alloc 3rd mmap");
+    close(fd); // Don't leak FD on failure
     munmap(base,size * 2);
     base = NULL;
   }
-  close(fd); // No longer needed after all memory maps are in place
   return base;
